WEBVTT

1
00:04:11.602 --> 00:04:14.238
Nurse Evelyn! Nurse Evelyn!

2
00:04:15.064 --> 00:04:18.116
I have a message for you. In English!

3
00:04:35.376 --> 00:04:37.668
And here we go.

4
00:04:37.669 --> 00:04:40.191
Now, look, here's the
list of all the patients

5
00:04:40.216 --> 00:04:42.415
we've had in the ward
in the last month.

6
00:04:49.390 --> 00:04:50.941
Thank you, Nurse.

7
00:05:58.083 --> 00:06:01.043
- You're Alexandria?
- Yes.

8
00:06:01.044 --> 00:06:05.339
Your note came in, and landed on my lap.

9
00:06:05.340 --> 00:06:07.633
Couldn't even understand it.
It's written in gibberish or something.

10
00:06:07.634 --> 00:06:12.689
You didn't understand it, you didn't
understand it. It's not for you.

11
00:06:16.727 --> 00:06:18.528
My name's Roy.

12
00:06:20.481 --> 00:06:23.200
- How'd you hurt your arm?
- I fell.

13
00:06:24.151 --> 00:06:25.234
Me too.

14
00:06:25.235 --> 00:06:27.370
I was picking oranges.

15
00:06:29.490 --> 00:06:31.166
Is that so?

16
00:06:33.410 --> 00:06:35.411
How do you go to the potty?

17
00:06:35.412 --> 00:06:38.581
I don't. They let me go right here.

18
00:06:38.582 --> 00:06:41.375
- In bed?
- Yeah, it's true.

19
00:06:41.376 --> 00:06:43.261
I don't believe.

20
00:06:44.671 --> 00:06:47.173
Hey, Alexandria.

21
00:06:47.174 --> 00:06:50.801
Hey, do you know
you're named after Alexander the Great

22
00:06:50.802 --> 00:06:53.679
who was the greatest warrior
who ever lived?

23
00:06:53.680 --> 00:06:57.517
Yes. And my note is not in gibberish.
It's in English!

24
00:06:57.518 --> 00:07:00.278
Hey, I can see you. Come on out here.

25
00:07:01.897 --> 00:07:04.074
I can see you hiding.

26
00:07:05.150 --> 00:07:06.743
Alexandria.

27
00:07:10.656 --> 00:07:14.292
Hey, did you know
he was also looking for a message?

28
00:07:17.955 --> 00:07:19.714
<i>He was lost.</i>

29
00:07:22.251 --> 00:07:27.013
<i>He almost died, separated from his army.</i>

30
00:07:28.006 --> 00:07:31.467
- Did he find the message?
- What?

31
00:07:31.468 --> 00:07:35.221
Did she find the message?
Alexandria the Great.

32
00:07:35.222 --> 00:07:38.275
All right, right, I'll tell you,
just come in here.

33
00:07:39.977 --> 00:07:42.654
Now, come on, grab that chair right there.

34
00:07:45.274 --> 00:07:48.201
All right, don't break your other arm.

35
00:07:53.156 --> 00:07:55.584
- Thank you.
- You're welcome.

36
00:08:00.581 --> 00:08:03.717
- What's in your box?
- Things I like.

37
00:08:05.460 --> 00:08:09.014
- Things you stole?
- No.

38
00:08:10.299 --> 00:08:11.975
A photo.

39
00:08:13.135 --> 00:08:15.645
Where'd you get the elephant?

40
00:08:16.430 --> 00:08:19.107
My friend gave it to me at work.

41
00:08:21.143 --> 00:08:23.111
He's from India.

42
00:08:23.854 --> 00:08:28.533
Look, this is my horse...

43
00:08:30.152 --> 00:08:33.496
- and this is my father.
- Yeah?

44
00:08:34.573 --> 00:08:37.783
He's got the same gap in his teeth,
must run in the family.

45
00:08:37.784 --> 00:08:40.536
- Yeah, and here is my house.
- Oh, yeah?

46
00:08:40.537 --> 00:08:43.122
- It was my house.
- What happened?

47
00:08:43.123 --> 00:08:46.009
- They burn it.
- Who burned it?

48
00:08:46.668 --> 00:08:48.386
Angry people.

49
00:08:50.005 --> 00:08:51.848
I'm sorry to hear that.

50
00:08:52.341 --> 00:08:54.935
I said, I'm sorry to hear that.

51
00:08:55.594 --> 00:08:56.886
Angry people.

52
00:08:56.887 --> 00:08:59.722
Yeah, I know,
I'm just sorry that your house got burned.

53
00:08:59.723 --> 00:09:02.058
Why did Alexander

54
00:09:02.059 --> 00:09:07.447
didn't go from that buildings on his horse?

55
00:09:08.231 --> 00:09:10.608
- If him was lost...
- What?

56
00:09:10.609 --> 00:09:15.797
Why did Alexander didn't go
from that middle of the buildings

57
00:09:16.698 --> 00:09:20.043
from that buildings on his horse?

58
00:09:21.078 --> 00:09:22.712
Well...

59
00:09:24.539 --> 00:09:30.139
<i>First of all, he didn't have a horse
because his horse was killed in a battle.</i>

60
00:09:33.340 --> 00:09:36.217
<i>And he wasn't
in the middle of any old buildings.</i>

61
00:09:36.218 --> 00:09:41.818
<i>He was lost in the middle of a vast desert,
full of orange sand</i>

62
00:09:42.641 --> 00:09:44.985
<i>with only a handful of men</i>

63
00:09:46.937 --> 00:09:49.698
<i>but they didn't have any water.</i>

64
00:10:12.170 --> 00:10:13.596
Look!

65
00:10:38.947 --> 00:10:42.324
<i>"My Lord, all hope is lost."</i>

66
00:10:42.325 --> 00:10:46.287
<i>"It seems your mighty army
shall finally be conquered."</i>

67
00:10:46.288 --> 00:10:51.667
<i>"Not by the Persians, but by our own greed
and gluttony for water."</i>

68
00:10:51.668 --> 00:10:54.971
<i>"This helmet contains our last supply."</i>

69
00:10:56.173 --> 00:10:59.809
<i>"Oh, King,
I believe your wisdom shall save us all."</i>

70
00:11:09.102 --> 00:11:10.519
- Why?
- Why?

71
00:11:10.520 --> 00:11:11.905
What?

72
00:11:13.023 --> 00:11:14.407
Why?

73
00:11:15.901 --> 00:11:19.820
Well, because there wasn't
enough water for all of them

74
00:11:19.821 --> 00:11:22.406
and it was Alexander the Great's way

75
00:11:22.407 --> 00:11:25.034
of showing his army
that they were all equal...

76
00:11:25.035 --> 00:11:26.952
It's stupid.

77
00:11:26.953 --> 00:11:28.370
What would you do better?

78
00:11:28.371 --> 00:11:31.040
Was Alexander throw the water

79
00:11:31.041 --> 00:11:36.096
instead to give every soldier a little bit.

80
00:11:42.344 --> 00:11:45.554
Hey, why don't you come back tomorrow
and I'm going to tell you a different story.

81
00:11:45.555 --> 00:11:49.475
An epic tale of love and revenge.

82
00:11:49.476 --> 00:11:51.852
- You know what "epic" means?
- No.

83
00:11:51.853 --> 00:11:54.146
I still got this tightness here.
It's like I can't even...

84
00:11:54.147 --> 00:11:57.566
It means a really long story,
and it's set in India.

85
00:11:57.567 --> 00:11:59.026
...the elephant sitting on my chest.

86
00:11:59.027 --> 00:12:01.028
- You should be fully recovered.
- All right, go on.

87
00:12:01.029 --> 00:12:03.030
- I want you to examine me.
- Will you come back tomorrow?

88
00:12:03.031 --> 00:12:06.084
You personally. I'm not very well.

89
00:12:13.917 --> 00:12:15.927
The swelling seems down.

90
00:12:17.754 --> 00:12:20.098
I know how much it hurts.

91
00:12:22.676 --> 00:12:25.177
A sense of humor.

92
00:12:25.178 --> 00:12:29.515
In the next couple of weeks the pain
should abate, then one more operation.

93
00:12:29.516 --> 00:12:31.350
Like the last one?

94
00:12:31.351 --> 00:12:34.436
This is going to take some effort
on your part, too, you know that?

95
00:12:34.437 --> 00:12:35.864
See?

96
00:13:23.403 --> 00:13:25.246
Come on, then.

97
00:13:46.593 --> 00:13:49.020
- Be back before lunch.
- Okay.

98
00:14:07.364 --> 00:14:09.990
Alexandria, get away from that ice.

99
00:14:09.991 --> 00:14:13.035
I see you licking that ice,
you're gonna get sick.

100
00:14:13.036 --> 00:14:15.079
I want you to go play, go!

101
00:14:15.080 --> 00:14:18.508
Next time, I'll glue your lips to this
and carry you away.

102
00:14:24.756 --> 00:14:27.383
You're lucky it was just a horse
that got killed.

103
00:14:27.384 --> 00:14:31.470
I mean, jumping off a train bridge
was suicide, too.

104
00:14:31.471 --> 00:14:33.856
And if you were trying to impress her...

105
00:14:34.516 --> 00:14:37.643
Sinclair already did a better job.

106
00:14:37.644 --> 00:14:39.696
You know, the actor,

107
00:14:41.064 --> 00:14:43.908
- the leading man.
- I know who he is.

108
00:14:44.985 --> 00:14:48.028
Every cloud has a silver lining,
that's for sure.

109
00:14:48.029 --> 00:14:49.154
Take another card.

110
00:14:49.155 --> 00:14:51.824
- You know, before my accident...
- That is the Queen of Hearts.

111
00:14:51.825 --> 00:14:53.242
...nothing was happening for me.

112
00:14:53.243 --> 00:14:56.912
Now I've had my leg hacked off by savages,

113
00:14:56.913 --> 00:15:00.749
mangled by chariots,
sawed off by lumberjacks.

114
00:15:00.750 --> 00:15:05.221
Hell, I've even had a harpoon through it.
I'm working all the time.

115
00:15:09.592 --> 00:15:11.844
That is the two of spades.

116
00:15:11.845 --> 00:15:14.888
- The studio is just trying to do right by you.
- Excuse me, Mr. Sabatini.

117
00:15:14.889 --> 00:15:17.099
Take the money.

118
00:15:17.100 --> 00:15:20.436
Anyway, gags are not for you, Roy.

119
00:15:20.437 --> 00:15:21.812
You're a college man.

120
00:15:21.813 --> 00:15:22.938
Wasn't me.

121
00:15:22.939 --> 00:15:24.907
One cripple to another...

122
00:15:26.401 --> 00:15:28.110
I didn't throw orange at you.

123
00:15:28.111 --> 00:15:30.496
...no woman is worth suicide.

124
00:15:31.614 --> 00:15:33.916
Like the guy's a movie star, for chrissake.

125
00:15:49.382 --> 00:15:51.934
Was your friend a pirate?

126
00:15:54.888 --> 00:15:57.440
Was your friend a pirate?

127
00:15:58.808 --> 00:16:00.485
Sometimes.

128
00:16:01.811 --> 00:16:05.147
Is that how he hurt his leg?

129
00:16:05.148 --> 00:16:09.318
No, he... He does tricks for pictures.

130
00:16:09.319 --> 00:16:12.154
You know, flickers.

131
00:16:12.155 --> 00:16:14.374
Moving pictures.

132
00:16:15.033 --> 00:16:18.461
- I never seen one.
- You're not missing much.

133
00:16:19.370 --> 00:16:22.298
Is that what you do, like your friend?

134
00:16:23.833 --> 00:16:25.551
Just once.

135
00:16:29.047 --> 00:16:31.682
Will you tell me the story now?

136
00:16:32.467 --> 00:16:35.311
- What story?
- The epic.

137
00:16:38.848 --> 00:16:40.483
All right.

138
00:16:42.602 --> 00:16:44.946
All right, close your eyes.

139
00:16:47.440 --> 00:16:49.325
What do you see?

140
00:16:50.527 --> 00:16:52.036
Nothing.

141
00:16:54.572 --> 00:16:56.165
Rub them.

142
00:16:57.659 --> 00:16:59.669
Can you see the stars?

143
00:17:00.870 --> 00:17:02.463
<i>Yes.</i>

144
00:17:02.872 --> 00:17:05.541
<i>It was a starry night.</i>

145
00:17:05.542 --> 00:17:10.379
<i>Four men waited impatiently
on a small island</i>

146
00:17:10.380 --> 00:17:13.423
<i>surrounded by a calm sea.</i>

147
00:17:13.424 --> 00:17:16.936
<i>But that calmness was deceptive.</i>

148
00:17:21.558 --> 00:17:23.892
<i>For at that moment</i>

149
00:17:23.893 --> 00:17:28.614
<i>an Indian with a bandaged thigh
swam towards them.</i>

150
00:17:35.238 --> 00:17:37.081
Tell me, Indian.

151
00:17:37.740 --> 00:17:39.542
Is it true?

152
00:17:42.495 --> 00:17:46.757
Luigi, is what true?

153
00:17:47.584 --> 00:17:51.929
Governor Odious will execute
your twin brother tomorrow morning.

154
00:17:52.881 --> 00:17:54.891
My poor brother.

155
00:18:00.805 --> 00:18:03.807
<i>In all, there were five of them.</i>

156
00:18:03.808 --> 00:18:06.560
<i>They had only one thing in common,</i>

157
00:18:06.561 --> 00:18:09.780
<i>a hatred of Governor Odious.</i>

158
00:18:11.107 --> 00:18:16.078
<i>The first was an ex-slave, Otta Benga.</i>

159
00:18:23.077 --> 00:18:27.122
<i>He and his brother were born into slavery</i>

160
00:18:27.123 --> 00:18:31.552
<i>only to fill the coffers
of the evil Governor Odious.</i>

161
00:18:33.338 --> 00:18:37.475
<i>One day while toiling in the fields...</i>

162
00:18:50.563 --> 00:18:55.359
<i>Heartbroken at his brother's death,
he freed the slaves</i>

163
00:18:55.360 --> 00:19:00.081
<i>and swore that he would be responsible
for Governor Odious's death.</i>

164
00:19:03.493 --> 00:19:04.952
<i>I like him.</i>

165
00:19:04.953 --> 00:19:08.330
<i>Then, there was the Indian,</i>

166
00:19:08.331 --> 00:19:12.468
<i>who, whenever anxious,
always stroked his brow.</i>

167
00:19:16.130 --> 00:19:21.730
<i>The Indian was supposedly married
to the most beautiful squaw in the world</i>

168
00:19:23.179 --> 00:19:25.889
<i>yet nobody had seen her.</i>

169
00:19:25.890 --> 00:19:30.394
<i>To verify this,
Odious disguised himself as a leper</i>

170
00:19:30.395 --> 00:19:34.699
<i>but when he saw her reflection,
he was smitten.</i>

171
00:19:37.944 --> 00:19:43.323
<i>Locking the doors to his Wigwam,
the Indian stood guard.</i>

172
00:19:43.324 --> 00:19:47.369
<i>Little did he know,
he was guarding an empty home</i>

173
00:19:47.370 --> 00:19:52.633
<i>for his wife had already been kidnapped
by the evil Governor Odious.</i>

174
00:19:53.918 --> 00:19:57.170
<i>But the squaw refused
to show herself to him.</i>

175
00:19:57.171 --> 00:20:01.350
<i>So, Odious had her thrown
into the Labyrinth of Despair.</i>

176
00:20:06.097 --> 00:20:10.109
<i>Eventually she realized
there was only one way out.</i>

177
00:20:25.658 --> 00:20:27.326
<i>While mourning his wife's death</i>

178
00:20:27.327 --> 00:20:30.954
<i>the Indian took a blood oath
never to look at another squaw</i>

179
00:20:30.955 --> 00:20:35.092
<i>and that he would be responsible
for Governor Odiousls death.</i>

180
00:20:39.464 --> 00:20:41.390
<i>I like him, too.</i>

181
00:20:41.674 --> 00:20:45.561
<i>Luigi was an explosive expert.</i>

182
00:20:47.930 --> 00:20:51.099
<i>When Odious heard
about the power of his new bombs,</i>

183
00:20:51.100 --> 00:20:53.653
<i>he had him publicly banished.</i>

184
00:20:54.145 --> 00:20:58.315
<i>On his return, Luigi discovered
that everybody hid from him</i>

185
00:20:58.316 --> 00:21:03.037
<i>because even speaking to him
was punishable by death.</i>

186
00:21:03.821 --> 00:21:07.240
<i>But when his own priest refused
to hear his confession,</i>

187
00:21:07.241 --> 00:21:12.841
<i>Luigi swore that he would be responsible
for Governor Odious's death!</i>

188
00:21:18.628 --> 00:21:22.556
<i>Next was the English naturalist</i>

189
00:21:23.257 --> 00:21:25.967
<i>Charles Darwin.</i>

190
00:21:25.968 --> 00:21:29.221
<i>He loved all living things,</i>

191
00:21:29.222 --> 00:21:34.443
<i>creatures, plants, everything alive.</i>

192
00:21:35.812 --> 00:21:40.190
<i>Darwin was always accompanied
by his shy, brilliant colleague,</i>

193
00:21:40.191 --> 00:21:41.483
<i>Wallace the monkey.</i>

194
00:21:41.484 --> 00:21:43.327
What is that, Wallace?

195
00:21:45.696 --> 00:21:47.489
I don't know why flamingos are pink.

196
00:21:47.490 --> 00:21:51.711
<i>Even though they had developed
many theories together</i>

197
00:21:52.328 --> 00:21:55.297
<i>they were still looking for something.</i>

198
00:21:56.582 --> 00:21:59.343
<i>- What?
- Butterfly.</i>

199
00:22:00.336 --> 00:22:02.388
<i>That's a good guess.</i>

200
00:22:02.839 --> 00:22:07.008
<i>In fact, a very specific butterfly</i>

201
00:22:07.009 --> 00:22:10.730
<i>called</i> Americana Exotica.

202
00:22:11.848 --> 00:22:15.568
<i>One day, Odious sent them a dead one.</i>

203
00:22:21.691 --> 00:22:23.617
<i>Butterfly Reef.</i>

204
00:22:25.736 --> 00:22:31.000
<i>This Odious, it's bad man?</i>

205
00:22:31.993 --> 00:22:33.544
<i>Oh, yeah.</i>

206
00:22:34.704 --> 00:22:36.505
<i>Butterfly Reef.</i>

207
00:22:37.248 --> 00:22:41.343
<i>That's where Governor Odious
chose to banish our heroes,</i>

208
00:22:42.462 --> 00:22:44.221
<i>to mock them,</i>

209
00:22:45.256 --> 00:22:50.561
<i>hoping that in their fight for survival
they would devour each other.</i>

210
00:22:51.888 --> 00:22:55.056
<i>So, the buccaneers
were trapped on this island.</i>

211
00:22:55.057 --> 00:22:57.193
<i>What means a buccaneer?</i>

212
00:22:57.810 --> 00:23:02.564
<i>Well, it's like a pirate. Pirate and
buccaneer, it's like the same thing.</i>

213
00:23:02.565 --> 00:23:05.242
But I don't like pirate stories.

214
00:23:06.402 --> 00:23:09.779
You're the one who asked for a pirate story.

215
00:23:09.780 --> 00:23:12.458
- No.
- Yes, you did.

216
00:23:14.035 --> 00:23:18.079
I just wanted to know
if your friend was a pirate.

217
00:23:18.080 --> 00:23:22.176
- Why?
- Because he has just one leg.

218
00:23:22.960 --> 00:23:24.970
Oh, right.

219
00:23:26.214 --> 00:23:30.726
Well, yeah, it's not a pirate story.
It's a story about bandits.

220
00:23:30.885 --> 00:23:34.814
<i>In fact, our masked hero
couldn't even swim.</i>

221
00:23:36.224 --> 00:23:38.526
I need to learn to swim.

222
00:23:42.688 --> 00:23:47.743
Finally, very little was known about
the gap-toothed Masked Bandit.

223
00:23:48.027 --> 00:23:50.913
<i>- Like my father?
- Yes, your father.</i>

224
00:23:52.907 --> 00:23:56.993
<i>Except that he and his twin brother,
the Blue Bandit,</i>

225
00:23:56.994 --> 00:24:01.090
<i>had escaped execution
from the Spanish Governor Odious.</i>

226
00:24:01.791 --> 00:24:05.919
<i>Knowing that their chances of survival
were better apart</i>

227
00:24:05.920 --> 00:24:08.463
<i>the two brothers separated</i>

228
00:24:08.464 --> 00:24:12.268
<i>swearing that
they would kill Governor Odious.</i>

229
00:24:16.764 --> 00:24:19.108
We must conceive a plan!

230
00:24:20.059 --> 00:24:23.946
I need to get off this island,
and rescue my twin brother.

231
00:24:30.570 --> 00:24:33.289
What? What?

232
00:24:35.866 --> 00:24:37.376
All elephants?

233
00:24:47.712 --> 00:24:49.763
I say, we...

234
00:24:56.220 --> 00:24:58.022
I have an idea.

235
00:25:31.047 --> 00:25:35.267
Darwin! That was a great idea!

236
00:25:51.901 --> 00:25:54.119
Come on, Otta Bengal

237
00:26:05.998 --> 00:26:10.594
Goodbye, my beautiful friend!
Have a nice swim!

238
00:26:16.467 --> 00:26:20.345
Darwin, you are a genius!

239
00:26:20.346 --> 00:26:21.930
Much obliged!

240
00:26:21.931 --> 00:26:24.692
Where do you get these ideas?

241
00:27:03.347 --> 00:27:05.524
What is it, my friend?

242
00:27:49.310 --> 00:27:54.323
How sad. The tortures of this world
have driven the poor man mad.

243
00:27:54.857 --> 00:27:56.900
Not true.

244
00:27:56.901 --> 00:28:00.120
He said he has been sent by his mystic cult

245
00:28:02.239 --> 00:28:06.293
to help us against Governor Odious
and his Spanish henchmen.

246
00:28:08.162 --> 00:28:14.009
This region was once a lush forest
alive with birds and sacred trees

247
00:28:17.546 --> 00:28:19.714
but Odious had them all burned down.

248
00:28:19.715 --> 00:28:25.178
He also says the birds are safe
inside his belly

249
00:28:25.179 --> 00:28:28.932
but we must take care
for only the fittest shall survive.

250
00:28:28.933 --> 00:28:32.319
Tell him we have no use of a mystic.

251
00:28:35.439 --> 00:28:37.658
We are on a dangerous mission.

252
00:28:39.151 --> 00:28:42.862
We need to hurry to the fort
to save my twin brother.

253
00:28:42.863 --> 00:28:45.207
He will only slow us down.

254
00:28:50.663 --> 00:28:52.214
Fish, <i>senor!</i>

255
00:30:26.634 --> 00:30:28.259
Stand aside, my friend.

256
00:30:28.260 --> 00:30:32.606
Before you say kaboom,
I have this door open.

257
00:31:16.100 --> 00:31:19.727
Forgive me, wise mystic, for my disrespect.

258
00:31:19.728 --> 00:31:23.532
Undoubtedly, you have a flair
for war-mongering.

259
00:31:24.984 --> 00:31:28.987
It would be my honor
if you consider joining us

260
00:31:28.988 --> 00:31:30.747
on our quest.

261
00:31:33.742 --> 00:31:36.128
We must save your brother!

262
00:31:44.712 --> 00:31:46.430
First,

263
00:31:50.676 --> 00:31:52.060
a little test.

264
00:31:52.219 --> 00:31:53.594
You can't stop there.

265
00:31:53.595 --> 00:31:58.474
I just wanna play a little game. I want you
to go outside and touch one of my toes.

266
00:31:58.475 --> 00:32:02.270
No, tell me the story.
What happened with the Blue Bandit?

267
00:32:02.271 --> 00:32:04.022
It won't take long.

268
00:32:04.023 --> 00:32:07.492
- Just go outside and touch one of my toes.
- Okay.

269
00:32:12.489 --> 00:32:14.615
- I'm touching your little toe.
- No!

270
00:32:14.616 --> 00:32:18.870
Please don't tell me
which toe you're touching. I gotta guess.

271
00:32:18.871 --> 00:32:21.873
That's the whole point of the game.
All right.

272
00:32:21.874 --> 00:32:23.842
I'm touching one.

273
00:32:28.964 --> 00:32:31.141
I'm touching one.

274
00:32:32.968 --> 00:32:35.395
You're touching my big toe?

275
00:32:38.307 --> 00:32:40.650
Are you telling the truth?

276
00:32:45.606 --> 00:32:47.157
Look.

277
00:32:50.402 --> 00:32:51.912
Really.

278
00:32:53.113 --> 00:32:55.448
Oh, I got that?

279
00:32:55.449 --> 00:32:57.283
What happened?

280
00:32:57.284 --> 00:32:59.243
What happened with his brother?
Did he save him?

281
00:32:59.244 --> 00:33:02.422
No, no, no, no. Were you telling a story?

282
00:33:03.248 --> 00:33:06.250
No, no, no.
Were you telling the truth just now?

283
00:33:06.251 --> 00:33:09.462
No. I was telling the truth.

284
00:33:09.463 --> 00:33:11.672
No. You just said no,
you weren't telling the truth.

285
00:33:11.673 --> 00:33:13.341
No, I tell you it.

286
00:33:13.342 --> 00:33:16.052
- Were you telling the truth?
- Yeah.

287
00:33:16.053 --> 00:33:18.605
When you just touched my toe?

288
00:33:21.016 --> 00:33:23.652
- You little liar.
- No.

289
00:33:26.146 --> 00:33:28.532
Alexandria, were you lying to me?

290
00:33:30.109 --> 00:33:32.202
I touch your big toe.

291
00:33:33.737 --> 00:33:35.664
We need to hurry!

292
00:33:36.657 --> 00:33:39.459
Do you want me to finish the story?

293
00:33:40.619 --> 00:33:44.589
<i>The Masked Bandit arrived
at the Chandelier Hall too late.</i>

294
00:33:46.041 --> 00:33:49.794
<i>Odious had already
tortured his brother and crew</i>

295
00:33:49.795 --> 00:33:51.596
<i>and hung them.</i>

296
00:34:09.523 --> 00:34:14.277
All right, that's it! It's not a circus.
It's not a playground for all your...

297
00:34:14.278 --> 00:34:16.955
Please! Are you listening to me?

298
00:34:17.239 --> 00:34:19.124
Get out of here!

299
00:34:19.366 --> 00:34:21.534
- You leave her alone.
- Come here, baby.

300
00:34:21.535 --> 00:34:23.628
Get off! Goddamn!

301
00:34:25.414 --> 00:34:29.676
No, no, no, sweetheart, come here,
come here. Come on.

302
00:35:26.475 --> 00:35:28.309
Dad?

303
00:35:28.310 --> 00:35:30.978
- Dad? Dad?
- I'm not feeling real well.

304
00:35:30.979 --> 00:35:32.230
- What do you want?
- He's doing it again.

305
00:35:32.231 --> 00:35:34.616
Will you stop that? Leave him alone!

306
00:36:03.929 --> 00:36:06.847
- What's that?
- Food.

307
00:36:06.848 --> 00:36:09.526
- Where'd you get it?
- The chapel.

308
00:36:14.856 --> 00:36:17.284
I'm sorry I shouted at you.

309
00:36:18.485 --> 00:36:20.653
I was angry.

310
00:36:20.654 --> 00:36:22.330
No problem.

311
00:36:23.031 --> 00:36:27.335
Are you trying to save my soul?
Are you trying to save my soul?

312
00:36:29.788 --> 00:36:31.747
- Do you understand me?
- What?

313
00:36:31.748 --> 00:36:34.959
- Did you understand what I meant?
- What you said?

314
00:36:34.960 --> 00:36:38.013
I said, are you trying to save my soul?

315
00:36:38.380 --> 00:36:41.048
- Giving me that.
- What mean that?

316
00:36:41.049 --> 00:36:43.685
The Eucharist. It's a...

317
00:36:44.761 --> 00:36:46.053
What?

318
00:36:46.054 --> 00:36:49.566
The Eucharist.
The thing you gave me. It's a...

319
00:36:50.309 --> 00:36:52.402
it saves your soul.

320
00:36:52.769 --> 00:36:56.355
The thing I gave to you, what?

321
00:36:56.356 --> 00:37:00.359
The little piece of bread
that you just gave me.

322
00:37:00.360 --> 00:37:02.370
It saves your soul.

323
00:37:02.821 --> 00:37:06.407
- What? What? What?
- Are you worried about me?

324
00:37:06.408 --> 00:37:09.076
Saves your soul.
Do you know what "soul" means?

325
00:37:09.077 --> 00:37:11.880
- No.
- It's like strength.

326
00:37:15.083 --> 00:37:19.137
Why does the old man
keep his teeth in a glass at night?

327
00:37:21.256 --> 00:37:25.644
It's where he keeps his
strength, his spirit.

328
00:37:26.762 --> 00:37:30.565
His spirit is in those teeth.

329
00:37:33.310 --> 00:37:34.819
Yeah.

330
00:37:35.270 --> 00:37:38.073
Oh, you're missing a little strength

331
00:37:38.982 --> 00:37:41.743
right in the front of your mouth.

332
00:37:44.780 --> 00:37:46.947
The chapel's in the main block, isn't it?

333
00:37:46.948 --> 00:37:49.793
Yes. What happened with the Black Bandit?

334
00:37:51.745 --> 00:37:53.463
I'm sorry.

335
00:37:55.123 --> 00:37:56.758
It's okay.

336
00:38:00.796 --> 00:38:03.089
They keep the medicine in the main block,
don't they?

337
00:38:03.090 --> 00:38:04.641
Yes.

338
00:38:24.653 --> 00:38:29.040
That which has been taken from me
can never be replaced.

339
00:38:30.325 --> 00:38:31.992
My brother...

340
00:38:31.993 --> 00:38:34.912
<i>- Why he speaks like this?
- Because he's your father.</i>

341
00:38:34.913 --> 00:38:37.090
<i>But my father is dead.</i>

342
00:38:37.958 --> 00:38:39.426
<i>What?</i>

343
00:38:40.877 --> 00:38:44.713
<i>Okay, how do you want me...
How do you want him to speak?</i>

344
00:38:44.714 --> 00:38:46.632
I think of all the joys we had.

345
00:38:46.633 --> 00:38:48.926
<i>Normal, like you.</i>

346
00:38:48.927 --> 00:38:51.813
I could've saved you, but I was weak.

347
00:38:53.473 --> 00:38:57.318
My grief has gone blood-red with revenge.

348
00:38:59.438 --> 00:39:01.489
I'm stronger now.

349
00:39:03.316 --> 00:39:09.216
I will search the four corners of this Earth,
find Governor Odious and joyously kill him!

350
00:39:12.784 --> 00:39:16.036
By the Blue Bandit's honor, I swear

351
00:39:16.037 --> 00:39:20.508
I will annihilate him
and everything that he loves!

352
00:39:26.756 --> 00:39:31.552
I will destroy him! I will destroy him!

353
00:39:31.553 --> 00:39:35.148
Destroy him! I will destroy him!

354
00:39:40.103 --> 00:39:42.781
And every Spanish thing.

355
00:39:43.773 --> 00:39:46.159
<i>I thought he was Spanish.</i>

356
00:39:46.818 --> 00:39:48.203
<i>No.</i>

357
00:39:49.446 --> 00:39:51.405
<i>He was French.</i>

358
00:39:51.406 --> 00:39:53.708
Are you with me, bandits?

359
00:40:16.264 --> 00:40:20.193
Darwin! Which way to Governor Odious?

360
00:40:21.102 --> 00:40:25.782
I tell him not to put the map with the bugs.

361
00:40:26.816 --> 00:40:28.108
Are we lost?

362
00:40:28.109 --> 00:40:29.536
<i>Sorry, Capitaine.</i>

363
00:40:30.570 --> 00:40:32.705
Hey! No!

364
00:40:35.408 --> 00:40:39.254
Hey! You can't eat it, it's poisonous!

365
00:40:47.462 --> 00:40:49.380
What's he saying?

366
00:40:49.381 --> 00:40:53.801
He says we should follow him
to greener pastures!

367
00:40:53.802 --> 00:40:57.897
- What?
- He say it's greener down there.

368
00:40:58.181 --> 00:41:00.808
Green? Down where?

369
00:41:00.809 --> 00:41:01.976
I don't know.

370
00:41:01.977 --> 00:41:04.186
To greener pastures!

371
00:41:04.187 --> 00:41:05.989
Slow down!

372
00:41:06.982 --> 00:41:11.286
The birds in his belly
crave greener pastures!

373
00:41:11.903 --> 00:41:15.415
Hey! It is greener down there.

374
00:41:16.199 --> 00:41:18.126
Greener pastures.

375
00:41:19.911 --> 00:41:21.629
Slow down!

376
00:41:31.464 --> 00:41:36.060
Please don't run!
The poison works faster if you run!

377
00:41:42.434 --> 00:41:44.068
Slow down.

378
00:41:54.321 --> 00:41:55.955
It's poisonous.

379
00:42:03.913 --> 00:42:05.465
What?

380
00:43:00.762 --> 00:43:02.814
He's giving us directions.

381
00:43:33.628 --> 00:43:34.971
Go!

382
00:44:28.850 --> 00:44:30.318
Slaves!

383
00:44:42.614 --> 00:44:44.665
Odious's flag.

384
00:44:50.538 --> 00:44:52.840
We must free the slaves.

385
00:45:07.514 --> 00:45:10.691
Tell me, Alexandria, do you read English?

386
00:45:11.059 --> 00:45:15.905
You always stop at the same part
when it's very beautiful

387
00:45:16.523 --> 00:45:18.273
and interesting.

388
00:45:18.274 --> 00:45:21.527
I just wanted to know
if you can read English.

389
00:45:21.528 --> 00:45:23.162
Can you?

390
00:45:23.905 --> 00:45:26.573
- Can you read English?
- Yeah.

391
00:45:26.574 --> 00:45:29.243
- What's this?
- Paper.

392
00:45:29.244 --> 00:45:32.120
No. What's this? This.

393
00:45:32.121 --> 00:45:36.843
M-o-r-p-h...

394
00:45:37.794 --> 00:45:39.753
Three.

395
00:45:39.754 --> 00:45:41.630
- What's that?
- Three.

396
00:45:41.631 --> 00:45:43.307
That's good.

397
00:45:46.052 --> 00:45:50.314
I'm having a hard time sleeping
and I can't remember that story.

398
00:45:52.851 --> 00:45:55.394
I need some pills.

399
00:45:55.395 --> 00:45:59.565
I need pills in a bottle
that has this written on them.

400
00:45:59.566 --> 00:46:02.776
M-o-r-p-h-i-n-three?

401
00:46:02.777 --> 00:46:06.038
Yes. And it's in the main block.

402
00:46:08.950 --> 00:46:11.586
In that room in the main block.

403
00:46:15.290 --> 00:46:16.832
You understand?

404
00:46:16.833 --> 00:46:20.460
- Ask the head nurse.
- I'm asking you as a friend.

405
00:46:20.461 --> 00:46:24.265
- But it's stealing.
- No, it's not. Not if you need it.

406
00:46:26.009 --> 00:46:29.604
It's no different
than stealing bread from a church.

407
00:46:31.806 --> 00:46:34.483
- I'll ask them for you.
- No.

408
00:46:35.894 --> 00:46:38.112
It's a bandit secret.

409
00:46:39.480 --> 00:46:43.159
I need the pills
to finish the story. Understand?

410
00:46:44.152 --> 00:46:46.454
- I can't get it...
- I'll do it.

411
00:46:47.363 --> 00:46:48.873
Thanks.

412
00:47:00.335 --> 00:47:02.470
You look beautiful.

413
00:47:04.839 --> 00:47:07.600
Why do you put red on your cheeks?

414
00:47:08.009 --> 00:47:13.856
Because it makes you look pretty

415
00:47:18.019 --> 00:47:20.738
and healthy, too.

416
00:47:23.983 --> 00:47:26.360
- Remember, back before lunch.
- I know!

417
00:47:26.361 --> 00:47:29.154
Alexandria, no licking the ice today?

418
00:47:29.155 --> 00:47:31.999
No. Thank you! Bye!

419
00:47:43.753 --> 00:47:46.722
One bite maybe. But a pit of snakes?

420
00:48:30.466 --> 00:48:36.266
M-o-r-p-h-i-n-three. M-o-r-p-h-i-n...

421
00:48:41.936 --> 00:48:44.405
M-o-r-p-h-i-n...

422
00:49:13.468 --> 00:49:18.972
Maybe you got...
I know it's important that you listen to me.

423
00:49:18.973 --> 00:49:21.275
You've gotta think of your other children.

424
00:49:21.726 --> 00:49:23.894
I'm so sorry.

425
00:49:23.895 --> 00:49:27.731
You have to warn your other children
about the sounds of rattlesnakes.

426
00:49:27.732 --> 00:49:32.870
This isn't a good time.
There are snake pits all over this area.

427
00:49:39.285 --> 00:49:42.996
Wake up! Wake up!
You better get up or they'll chop you.

428
00:49:42.997 --> 00:49:47.334
You get up! You better get up
and show these people you are sleeping.

429
00:49:47.335 --> 00:49:50.837
These men will chop you if you don't get up.
Get up!

430
00:49:50.838 --> 00:49:53.641
Get up. This isn't funny.

431
00:49:54.425 --> 00:49:57.061
Please, let's leave this place.

432
00:50:09.941 --> 00:50:12.159
Come on. Come on!

433
00:50:18.741 --> 00:50:21.201
I do that all the time.

434
00:50:21.202 --> 00:50:26.424
All you have to do is change your clothes
and hide the wet ones until they're dry.

435
00:50:29.377 --> 00:50:32.879
You know what I do
when something frightens me?

436
00:50:32.880 --> 00:50:35.057
I say the magic words.

437
00:50:37.009 --> 00:50:41.564
Googly, googly, googly, begone.

438
00:50:45.059 --> 00:50:47.727
Let's practice together.

439
00:50:47.728 --> 00:50:49.697
The magic words.

440
00:50:50.231 --> 00:50:53.576
Googly, googly, googly. Go away.

441
00:51:00.700 --> 00:51:04.128
- Did you get what I sent you for?
- Yes.

442
00:51:05.746 --> 00:51:07.882
- This it is.
- Yeah?

443
00:51:09.667 --> 00:51:11.626
There's only three in here.

444
00:51:11.627 --> 00:51:14.796
- You asked me for three.
- No, I asked you for a full bottle.

445
00:51:14.797 --> 00:51:18.476
- But, you wrote...
- Was this bottle full of pills?

446
00:51:19.802 --> 00:51:21.845
- Were there more pills in here?
- Yeah.

447
00:51:21.846 --> 00:51:23.180
What did you do with them?

448
00:51:23.181 --> 00:51:26.108
I throw them in toilet.

449
00:51:27.435 --> 00:51:30.604
But I throw them away because you wrote

450
00:51:30.605 --> 00:51:35.701
m-o-r-p-h-i-n-three.

451
00:51:38.696 --> 00:51:41.165
Will they help you sleep?

452
00:51:44.660 --> 00:51:46.420
A nap perhaps.

453
00:51:53.044 --> 00:51:54.252
<i>We must free the slaves.</i>

454
00:51:54.253 --> 00:51:56.555
Did they free the slaves?

455
00:53:14.292 --> 00:53:16.218
Come out, Odious.

456
00:53:39.400 --> 00:53:41.368
Just like a butterfly.

457
00:53:47.074 --> 00:53:49.909
<i>Why the mask again?</i>

458
00:53:49.910 --> 00:53:52.787
<i>He doesn't want to scare her.</i>

459
00:53:52.788 --> 00:53:58.093
<i>She doesn't know anything about him,
but he knew everything about her.</i>

460
00:54:00.004 --> 00:54:03.390
<i>The color of her eyes.</i>

461
00:54:04.675 --> 00:54:05.976
<i>Brown.</i>

462
00:54:06.594 --> 00:54:09.220
<i>Her favorite food.</i>

463
00:54:09.221 --> 00:54:10.597
<i>Orange?</i>

464
00:54:10.598 --> 00:54:12.766
<i>Her favorite book.</i>

465
00:54:12.767 --> 00:54:14.234
<i>Bible.</i>

466
00:54:15.019 --> 00:54:18.405
Boys, she's mine.

467
00:54:22.610 --> 00:54:24.319
<i>- What about the bomb?
- What?</i>

468
00:54:24.320 --> 00:54:25.913
<i>The bomb.</i>

469
00:54:34.497 --> 00:54:39.802
<i>The bandits kidnapped the princess,
leaving behind her little nephew.</i>

470
00:54:46.467 --> 00:54:49.052
<i>They rode down
from the high mountain deserts</i>

471
00:54:49.053 --> 00:54:51.105
<i>to a place he loved.</i>

472
00:54:54.308 --> 00:54:57.653
<i>He had played as a child with his twin.</i>

473
00:54:59.522 --> 00:55:02.449
<i>A palace in the middle of a lake.</i>

474
00:55:43.315 --> 00:55:46.326
What's the matter with that poor fellow?

475
00:55:48.279 --> 00:55:50.655
Ever since the Indian's misfortune

476
00:55:50.656 --> 00:55:53.783
he took a vow
to never look at another squaw.

477
00:55:53.784 --> 00:55:58.088
But a man cannot show what's in his heart
when he hides his face.

478
00:56:00.207 --> 00:56:02.750
Who, may I ask, are you?

479
00:56:02.751 --> 00:56:05.879
To most I am known as the Masked Bandit.

480
00:56:05.880 --> 00:56:08.390
The Scourge of the Southeast?

481
00:56:10.926 --> 00:56:12.770
That's the one.

482
00:56:17.892 --> 00:56:20.819
But that's only when I wear the mask.

483
00:56:28.402 --> 00:56:30.162
Who are you?

484
00:56:34.909 --> 00:56:36.668
Nurse Evelyn.

485
00:56:39.413 --> 00:56:44.593
Once I was Lady Evelyn Everest Everhardt,
and now I am simply called...

486
00:56:44.793 --> 00:56:47.420
- Sister Evelyn.
- She is not a sister.

487
00:56:47.421 --> 00:56:50.766
Bless you. No. What? Yes, she is.

488
00:56:51.467 --> 00:56:54.603
She doesn't have brothers and sisters.

489
00:56:55.304 --> 00:56:58.649
No, she's a nun, like these nuns out here.

490
00:57:03.020 --> 00:57:05.480
And she turned from the Masked Bandit,
and she said...

491
00:57:05.481 --> 00:57:08.826
- May I be frank with you?
- Of course.

492
00:57:09.443 --> 00:57:12.403
Although I've dedicated my life
to God and goodness

493
00:57:12.404 --> 00:57:16.866
I secretly love throwing oranges
at our priest.

494
00:57:16.867 --> 00:57:19.452
Take two turns to the left
and go to the bathroom.

495
00:57:19.453 --> 00:57:20.912
No, you read my note.

496
00:57:20.913 --> 00:57:23.331
What are you talking about?
Go to the bathroom.

497
00:57:23.332 --> 00:57:25.208
No.

498
00:57:25.209 --> 00:57:27.627
How do you know
about the priest and the orange?

499
00:57:27.628 --> 00:57:30.171
Everybody knows
you like throwing oranges at the priest.

500
00:57:30.172 --> 00:57:34.425
Even the priest knows, but I didn't
find that out from your gibberish message.

501
00:57:34.426 --> 00:57:36.478
It's not gibberish.

502
00:58:03.747 --> 00:58:07.208
She wants to ask you
how much days I have to stay here.

503
00:58:07.209 --> 00:58:10.345
Well, I want you to stay here
until you get better.

504
00:58:12.548 --> 00:58:15.967
Her cast will come off in a few days

505
00:58:15.968 --> 00:58:20.439
but I'd like her to stay here
until she's completely recovered.

506
00:58:29.273 --> 00:58:32.066
She wants to say
that we are spend here too much times

507
00:58:32.067 --> 00:58:33.985
and we have to leave the city.

508
00:58:33.986 --> 00:58:38.281
No, well, you just tell her
that you shouldn't be working in the groves.

509
00:58:38.282 --> 00:58:40.074
That at your age it's dangerous

510
00:58:40.075 --> 00:58:43.119
and you'll spend
the rest of your days picking fruit.

511
00:58:43.120 --> 00:58:46.048
And then she'll fall. She surely will fall.

512
00:59:12.232 --> 00:59:13.867
Thank you.

513
00:59:14.985 --> 00:59:18.038
- What did she say?
- She says okay.

514
00:59:19.114 --> 00:59:20.615
- Really?
- Really.

515
00:59:20.616 --> 00:59:22.742
Alexandria, she asked me something,
didn't she?

516
00:59:22.743 --> 00:59:24.920
No, that how we speak.

517
00:59:26.455 --> 00:59:28.382
- You sure?
- Sure.

518
00:59:45.933 --> 00:59:51.488
Beautiful machina. Beautiful machina.

519
01:00:07.121 --> 01:00:11.800
Beautiful machina. Beautiful machina.

520
01:00:14.128 --> 01:00:18.381
Beautiful machina. Beautiful machina.

521
01:00:18.382 --> 01:00:20.800
It's a very generous offer.

522
01:00:20.801 --> 01:00:25.805
If you look over here at the number,
it's more money than I actually make a year.

523
01:00:25.806 --> 01:00:27.557
I want to add something to it.

524
01:00:27.558 --> 01:00:29.559
Don't start adding stuff to this.

525
01:00:29.560 --> 01:00:33.312
You know, the studio's got
a building full of lawyers.

526
01:00:33.313 --> 01:00:36.441
Jumping, falling, crashing.

527
01:00:36.442 --> 01:00:39.286
I mean, cowhands are getting all the glory.

528
01:00:40.320 --> 01:00:42.989
Whose idea was it anyway?

529
01:00:42.990 --> 01:00:46.126
Jumping onto a horse from a train bridge?

530
01:00:48.912 --> 01:00:52.331
Add the screening to the contract
and I'll sign it.

531
01:00:52.332 --> 01:00:54.625
What happens to the money if I die?

532
01:00:54.626 --> 01:00:59.264
Roy, you need to get off this suicide thing.

533
01:01:00.799 --> 01:01:03.977
Let the doctors finish what they started.

534
01:01:05.304 --> 01:01:07.647
Problem is not his back.

535
01:01:09.016 --> 01:01:11.151
It's a broken heart.

536
01:01:12.728 --> 01:01:14.562
He needs to get over her.

537
01:01:14.563 --> 01:01:17.991
I mean, he's not the first guy
to lose a girl.

538
01:01:19.401 --> 01:01:21.036
I'm sorry.

539
01:01:22.738 --> 01:01:24.998
You are someone famous.

540
01:01:26.867 --> 01:01:28.326
So they tell me.

541
01:01:28.327 --> 01:01:29.961
Hey, kid!

542
01:01:42.216 --> 01:01:44.309
I made this for you.

543
01:01:51.558 --> 01:01:53.184
Who's in the mask?

544
01:01:53.185 --> 01:01:56.363
You in the wheelchair.

545
01:02:00.025 --> 01:02:02.035
It's beautiful.

546
01:02:03.445 --> 01:02:05.404
I'll keep it forever.

547
01:02:05.405 --> 01:02:08.125
I hope I never get better.

548
01:02:09.868 --> 01:02:15.090
- Why?
- Because I want to stay here with you.

549
01:02:23.590 --> 01:02:26.518
- Hey, this came for you today.
- Really?

550
01:02:28.470 --> 01:02:31.648
- You like chocolate?
- I like it.

551
01:02:35.102 --> 01:02:38.864
- Do you want me to finish the story?
- Yes.

552
01:02:40.983 --> 01:02:44.077
- I need a favor.
- What kind of favor?

553
01:02:44.778 --> 01:02:46.237
You know our friend Walt?

554
01:02:46.238 --> 01:02:49.407
- He's not my friend.
- He's not my friend either.

555
01:02:49.408 --> 01:02:55.255
I retrieved this key from him
because I think he's been stealing my pills.

556
01:02:56.290 --> 01:02:59.509
I think he's got them in his cabinet there.

557
01:02:59.835 --> 01:03:02.920
I want you to go check
and see if he's got them.

558
01:03:02.921 --> 01:03:05.724
Why? I got you the bottle.

559
01:03:06.341 --> 01:03:09.936
There weren't enough in there
for me to go to sleep.

560
01:03:14.057 --> 01:03:17.027
Come on. Be a good bandit.

561
01:03:20.063 --> 01:03:22.490
I don't want to be a bandit.

562
01:03:23.984 --> 01:03:25.785
That's too bad.

563
01:03:26.820 --> 01:03:32.292
<i>Because Odious's castle
is surrounded by a big blue city.</i>

564
01:03:35.203 --> 01:03:39.799
<i>And that's where the bandits are headed
for their final encounter.</i>

565
01:03:43.754 --> 01:03:46.422
It's the best part of the story,
and since you're leaving soon

566
01:03:46.423 --> 01:03:50.977
I'd hate for you to spend your whole life
wondering how it turned out.

567
01:03:54.765 --> 01:03:57.350
- What's in the drawer?
- Stuff.

568
01:03:57.351 --> 01:04:01.279
- What kind of stuff?
- Stuff Walt's been stealing from me.

569
01:04:02.230 --> 01:04:04.023
What?

570
01:04:04.024 --> 01:04:06.108
I won't know until you go look.

571
01:04:06.109 --> 01:04:09.663
- Promise you'll finish the story?
- Yeah.

572
01:04:34.471 --> 01:04:36.439
It's that brown bottle.

573
01:04:37.975 --> 01:04:41.069
- This one?
- That's the one.

574
01:04:42.020 --> 01:04:44.489
I think he stole it from me.

575
01:04:50.821 --> 01:04:52.372
That's mine.

576
01:04:54.449 --> 01:04:56.659
<i>Where did we leave off?</i>

577
01:04:56.660 --> 01:04:58.619
<i>They were telling secrets each other.</i>

578
01:04:58.620 --> 01:05:01.589
I'm looking for the man
who murdered my father.

579
01:05:02.791 --> 01:05:03.916
<i>The Black Bandit said.</i>

580
01:05:03.917 --> 01:05:06.219
My brother, the Blue Masked Bandit...

581
01:05:07.170 --> 01:05:09.171
<i>- He said:</i>
- ...tried to avenge our father's death.

582
01:05:09.172 --> 01:05:13.968
<i>I've been on a quest for revenge.</i>

583
01:05:13.969 --> 01:05:15.219
Tortured and hung.

584
01:05:15.220 --> 01:05:20.808
<i>He told her everything about his life
except for the name of Governor Odious.</i>

585
01:05:20.809 --> 01:05:22.819
You need to leave.

586
01:05:31.361 --> 01:05:33.204
<i>You should go.</i>

587
01:05:33.488 --> 01:05:36.624
<i>But you promised you'll tell me the story.</i>

588
01:05:41.288 --> 01:05:44.090
You've captivated my heart, Evelyn.

589
01:05:45.959 --> 01:05:49.429
That's why
I can no longer keep you in captivity.

590
01:05:50.630 --> 01:05:53.183
I've fallen in love with you.

591
01:05:54.634 --> 01:05:57.270
But I am consumed with revenge.

592
01:05:59.806 --> 01:06:02.692
I'm not a man who can be loved.

593
01:06:03.477 --> 01:06:06.154
When I fall asleep, you gotta go.

594
01:06:09.316 --> 01:06:11.826
And don't come back tomorrow.

595
01:06:13.028 --> 01:06:14.454
Okay.

596
01:06:18.742 --> 01:06:20.418
Thank you.

597
01:06:27.459 --> 01:06:30.136
- I'm sorry about this.
- Why?

598
01:06:34.382 --> 01:06:36.142
I'm sorry.

599
01:06:38.553 --> 01:06:40.063
Why?

600
01:06:42.349 --> 01:06:45.193
I don't want you to see me like this.

601
01:06:49.856 --> 01:06:52.492
You think you took me captive?

602
01:06:56.863 --> 01:06:59.916
In fact, you're my savior.

603
01:07:04.913 --> 01:07:08.675
I was like a bird in a golden cage.

604
01:07:12.045 --> 01:07:15.598
By freeing me, you captured my heart.

605
01:07:25.392 --> 01:07:27.143
<i>Make them kiss.</i>

606
01:07:27.144 --> 01:07:30.029
<i>No, I don't want to make them kiss.</i>

607
01:07:31.523 --> 01:07:32.991
<i>Why?</i>

608
01:07:33.400 --> 01:07:36.369
<i>Because what they're about to find out.</i>

609
01:07:42.325 --> 01:07:45.211
She should have not come with us.

610
01:07:47.289 --> 01:07:50.624
- Why?
- It is too dangerous.

611
01:07:50.625 --> 01:07:55.430
If we are captured,
Governor Odious shall surely kill her.

612
01:07:57.090 --> 01:07:59.392
You mentioned Odious?

613
01:08:00.594 --> 01:08:02.645
He is my sworn enemy.

614
01:08:03.180 --> 01:08:04.981
And my fiancé.

615
01:08:33.043 --> 01:08:34.385
No.

616
01:08:37.297 --> 01:08:40.099
I want to look at you until I die.

617
01:08:43.261 --> 01:08:46.222
What a mystery this world.

618
01:08:46.223 --> 01:08:48.766
One day you love them

619
01:08:48.767 --> 01:08:52.946
and the next day
you want to kill them a thousand times over.

620
01:08:56.316 --> 01:08:58.284
God forgive him.

621
01:09:05.492 --> 01:09:07.919
I'm glad I never kissed you.

622
01:09:14.459 --> 01:09:16.261
<i>She can't die.</i>

623
01:09:20.340 --> 01:09:22.308
She's still alive!

624
01:09:29.266 --> 01:09:32.402
The solid gold locket stopped the bullet.

625
01:09:41.111 --> 01:09:44.029
"My dearest daughter,"

626
01:09:44.030 --> 01:09:49.919
"never marry for money, fame,
power or security."

627
01:09:51.162 --> 01:09:54.999
"Always follow your heart."

628
01:09:55.000 --> 01:09:56.750
"Your ever-loving father."

629
01:09:56.751 --> 01:09:59.846
it says all that on that little locket?

630
01:10:02.590 --> 01:10:04.591
I've never been able to open it.

631
01:10:04.592 --> 01:10:08.479
No one's been able to open it.
You're the first.

632
01:10:12.183 --> 01:10:16.562
And he knew that she was the woman
he was supposed to love.

633
01:10:16.563 --> 01:10:20.408
Please. Please. Now they can kiss-kiss?

634
01:10:21.443 --> 01:10:22.869
Yes.

635
01:10:25.363 --> 01:10:27.707
But first, marriage.

636
01:10:32.454 --> 01:10:34.756
And then they can kiss.

637
01:10:54.267 --> 01:10:55.902
The ring.

638
01:11:20.794 --> 01:11:23.796
The Mystic spies danger in your palm.

639
01:11:23.797 --> 01:11:27.392
You've taken too many pills. Death is near.

640
01:11:29.135 --> 01:11:30.469
Danger?

641
01:11:30.470 --> 01:11:33.106
Suicide is not the answer.

642
01:11:34.933 --> 01:11:38.519
He says he also knows of a secret chant.

643
01:11:38.520 --> 01:11:40.446
Whenever we're in trouble...

644
01:11:42.023 --> 01:11:45.535
Something about "googly-googly?"

645
01:11:47.028 --> 01:11:50.623
He says if you fall asleep,
you will never wake up.

646
01:12:16.266 --> 01:12:18.517
<i>The Mystic was right.</i>

647
01:12:18.518 --> 01:12:21.654
<i>The stony-faced priest had betrayed them.</i>

648
01:13:27.504 --> 01:13:29.838
<i>And then they were saved?</i>

649
01:13:29.839 --> 01:13:31.224
<i>No.</i>

650
01:13:36.596 --> 01:13:39.440
<i>There was no one left to save them.</i>

651
01:13:51.528 --> 01:13:53.079
Wallace?

652
01:13:54.656 --> 01:13:58.283
Wallace, is that you? Wallace?

653
01:13:58.284 --> 01:14:00.086
No, it's me.

654
01:14:05.917 --> 01:14:08.845
No wonder the bag was so heavy.

655
01:14:26.187 --> 01:14:27.697
Shoot!

656
01:14:33.278 --> 01:14:35.955
Shoot! Shoot! Shoot them, Daddy!

657
01:14:37.657 --> 01:14:39.458
Shoot them!

658
01:14:44.330 --> 01:14:47.499
Daddy, don't you recognize me?

659
01:14:47.500 --> 01:14:49.510
Don't you? It's me!

660
01:14:51.921 --> 01:14:54.140
Don't you recognize me?

661
01:14:58.261 --> 01:15:01.263
- Who are you?
- It's me, Da-da.

662
01:15:01.264 --> 01:15:03.348
- Who?
- Me!

663
01:15:03.349 --> 01:15:06.485
- My daughter?
- Yes! You recognize me.

664
01:15:07.562 --> 01:15:11.189
Yeah. My daughter
from a previous marriage.

665
01:15:11.190 --> 01:15:12.909
Yes.

666
01:15:15.778 --> 01:15:19.123
I didn't recognize you
because you have teeth.

667
01:15:21.951 --> 01:15:24.420
You must be stronger now.

668
01:15:26.914 --> 01:15:29.508
Not the time to sleep now.

669
01:15:31.085 --> 01:15:33.304
Not the time to sleep.

670
01:15:37.634 --> 01:15:39.852
It's not time to sleep.

671
01:16:00.531 --> 01:16:02.083
Wake up.

672
01:16:10.917 --> 01:16:13.135
Wake up. It's not time to sleep now.

673
01:16:17.048 --> 01:16:18.557
Wake up.

674
01:16:20.134 --> 01:16:21.936
Don't pretend to sleep.

675
01:16:22.929 --> 01:16:25.731
Wake up. Laugh, laugh.

676
01:16:31.062 --> 01:16:33.239
Not the time to sleep.

677
01:17:31.622 --> 01:17:36.761
<i>Americana Exotica.</i>

678
01:17:41.299 --> 01:17:43.559
Does Dr. Snider know about this?

679
01:17:53.102 --> 01:17:56.772
He was under observation,
but I thought he was getting better.

680
01:17:56.773 --> 01:17:58.157
Hey!

681
01:17:58.858 --> 01:18:02.152
Alexandria, go inside! Go on!

682
01:18:02.153 --> 01:18:05.122
All right, carry on. Sorry about that.

683
01:18:23.841 --> 01:18:26.811
Roy, wake up. Wake up.

684
01:18:27.678 --> 01:18:29.814
Roy, wake up.

685
01:18:32.183 --> 01:18:35.852
They're going to out you up.
Gonna chop you up. Wake up.

686
01:18:35.853 --> 01:18:38.489
- Go on! Shoo!
- Wake up.

687
01:18:42.985 --> 01:18:44.069
Oh, no, no, no.

688
01:18:44.070 --> 01:18:47.072
He was his usual self, you know,
smiling away, playing with his teeth.

689
01:18:47.073 --> 01:18:49.866
I just don't feel very well, Doc.

690
01:18:49.867 --> 01:18:53.379
I don't know
what the hell's wrong with me. Cough.

691
01:18:54.539 --> 01:18:56.748
What, am I going delirious
from the medication?

692
01:18:56.749 --> 01:18:59.260
I don't know what the hell...

693
01:19:03.881 --> 01:19:05.224
Roy!

694
01:19:06.175 --> 01:19:10.720
Roy, I thought you were dead.

695
01:19:10.721 --> 01:19:14.599
Saw two men,
and they were carrying the body away.

696
01:19:14.600 --> 01:19:17.778
And then I tried to pinch your toe.

697
01:19:21.524 --> 01:19:23.692
I run after you,

698
01:19:23.693 --> 01:19:29.281
and after that one of the doctors told me,
"Shoo!" and I had to go away.

699
01:19:29.782 --> 01:19:33.752
I'm sorry. I promise, but you...

700
01:19:39.000 --> 01:19:42.043
- I bring you more medicine if you want.
- Sugar.

701
01:19:42.044 --> 01:19:44.337
- I promise...
- They're giving him sugar.

702
01:19:44.338 --> 01:19:46.140
Come here!

703
01:19:46.757 --> 01:19:51.386
Oh, well, that's great, you're awake.
I brought your x-rays...

704
01:19:51.387 --> 01:19:53.722
- Hey, you wanna take a look...
- Doc, the old man's dead and you're...

705
01:19:53.723 --> 01:19:55.691
- Hey. Roy!
- That's it!

706
01:19:56.642 --> 01:19:58.894
- Will you shut up, already?
- You shut up!

707
01:19:58.895 --> 01:20:02.314
Get out of here! You're not really sick,
Walt! They're feeding you sugar!

708
01:20:02.315 --> 01:20:04.608
- Hey, hey, hey, hey, hey!
- I've had enough of you!

709
01:20:04.609 --> 01:20:05.692
Nurse!

710
01:20:05.693 --> 01:20:07.444
What do you mean, they're giving me sugar?

711
01:20:07.445 --> 01:20:09.821
- Here you go, Doctor.
- She's wet herself.

712
01:20:09.822 --> 01:20:11.957
Get her out of here.

713
01:20:14.368 --> 01:20:17.046
Go back to your room. Orderlies!

714
01:21:11.550 --> 01:21:13.635
You should be in bed, Alexandria.

715
01:21:13.636 --> 01:21:16.438
There's more fires in the field.

716
01:21:19.767 --> 01:21:23.979
It's kerosene.
The kerosene stops the fruit from freezing.

717
01:21:23.980 --> 01:21:27.732
No, it's Mystic.

718
01:21:27.733 --> 01:21:30.995
He's coming out of that tree to help Roy.

719
01:21:32.655 --> 01:21:36.834
I think it's bedtime, young lady.
No more time for funny talk.

720
01:21:37.618 --> 01:21:39.378
Into bed now.

721
01:21:40.162 --> 01:21:41.579
And maybe one day

722
01:21:41.580 --> 01:21:45.759
you can take me downstairs
and introduce me to your friend Roy.

723
01:21:46.544 --> 01:21:49.587
We go downstairs and say good night?

724
01:21:49.588 --> 01:21:52.683
No. He's not allowed any visitors.

725
01:21:53.426 --> 01:21:56.177
Your friend, Roy, needs to rest.

726
01:21:56.178 --> 01:22:00.473
He's very sad. He's lost his girlfriend.
He needs to sleep.

727
01:22:00.474 --> 01:22:04.978
But he can't. He needs medicine to sleep,
but he doesn't have any.

728
01:22:04.979 --> 01:22:06.271
That's the problem.

729
01:22:06.272 --> 01:22:10.159
I'm sure
they're taking very good care of him.

730
01:22:10.943 --> 01:22:13.245
Now, it's time for bed.

731
01:22:14.280 --> 01:22:16.823
Little girls need to go to sleep, too.

732
01:22:16.824 --> 01:22:19.835
- I'm not little. I am five.
- Of course.

733
01:22:20.453 --> 01:22:22.087
I forgot.

734
01:23:20.096 --> 01:23:25.934
Googly, googly, googly, go away.
Googly, googly, googly, go away.

735
01:23:25.935 --> 01:23:30.030
Googly, googly, googly, go away.
Googly, googly, googly, go away.

736
01:23:34.026 --> 01:23:39.373
Googly, googly. Go away.
Googly, googly, googly. Go away.

737
01:23:56.799 --> 01:24:00.552
Googly, googly. Go away.

738
01:24:00.553 --> 01:24:05.065
Googly, googly.
Googly, googly, googly, go away.

739
01:24:28.789 --> 01:24:33.385
<i>Papa, they steal our horse.</i>

740
01:24:35.963 --> 01:24:40.267
<i>Papa, they steal our horse.</i>

741
01:24:41.093 --> 01:24:42.644
<i>Papa,</i>

742
01:24:46.348 --> 01:24:48.641
<i>they steal our horse.</i>

743
01:24:48.642 --> 01:24:52.687
<i>Papa, angry people burn our home.</i>

744
01:24:52.688 --> 01:24:55.940
<i>They burn our house. Don't go outside.</i>

745
01:24:55.941 --> 01:24:57.284
Thieves.

746
01:24:58.027 --> 01:25:00.496
<i>Angry people kill.</i>

747
01:25:01.322 --> 01:25:03.123
Thieves!

748
01:25:35.147 --> 01:25:36.907
<i>The x-ray seems fine.</i>

749
01:25:55.251 --> 01:25:58.303
<i>- Mommy!
- Were you taking medicine to Roy?</i>

750
01:26:00.339 --> 01:26:04.717
<i>That is your responsibility
and this is how you treat it.</i>

751
01:26:04.718 --> 01:26:08.105
<i>To get better, you gotta have the will</i>

752
01:26:09.515 --> 01:26:11.817
and your own desire to live.

753
01:26:49.388 --> 01:26:51.639
I fell again.

754
01:26:51.640 --> 01:26:54.651
I heard. Everybody's heard.

755
01:26:56.437 --> 01:26:58.280
You're famous.

756
01:27:02.985 --> 01:27:04.736
Are they angry?

757
01:27:04.737 --> 01:27:06.330
Yeah,

758
01:27:08.615 --> 01:27:10.033
but not at you.

759
01:27:10.034 --> 01:27:14.787
I try to take more pills, but I fell.
It was the wrong thing, and...

760
01:27:14.788 --> 01:27:19.292
- What?
- I put my foot on it when I went up

761
01:27:19.293 --> 01:27:25.391
and later on the thing
made me go like that

762
01:27:25.392 --> 01:27:27.492
and I fell.

763
01:27:33.515 --> 01:27:37.069
I didn't tell anybody about our secret.

764
01:27:39.063 --> 01:27:42.824
Even when they tortured me with needles.

765
01:27:44.985 --> 01:27:47.579
Is that a pirate's flag?

766
01:27:49.365 --> 01:27:51.458
Is that yes or no?

767
01:27:52.409 --> 01:27:54.419
Tell me the story.

768
01:27:54.912 --> 01:27:57.080
I should go. You need your rest.

769
01:27:57.081 --> 01:27:58.748
But I want to talk.

770
01:27:58.749 --> 01:28:01.301
- I know you do.
- You promised.

771
01:28:02.461 --> 01:28:06.297
The story was just a trick
to get you to do something for me.

772
01:28:06.298 --> 01:28:08.600
- What?
- I was...

773
01:28:10.344 --> 01:28:13.063
But I need the story.

774
01:28:14.640 --> 01:28:17.275
You should ask someone else.

775
01:28:18.268 --> 01:28:21.113
There's no happy ending with me.

776
01:28:23.816 --> 01:28:25.701
I still want to know.

777
01:28:27.569 --> 01:28:29.821
Ask your friend, Nurse Evelyn,
she'll tell it better than I will.

778
01:28:29.822 --> 01:28:32.156
I don't want her in the story!

779
01:28:32.157 --> 01:28:33.875
She's okay.

780
01:28:35.327 --> 01:28:39.005
Oh, she doesn't really
love Governor Odious.

781
01:28:39.498 --> 01:28:43.084
She's just pretending.

782
01:28:43.085 --> 01:28:46.504
I saw her with one of the hospital men.

783
01:28:46.505 --> 01:28:49.349
She was just pretending to love you.

784
01:28:53.679 --> 01:28:55.847
Just like your girlfriend.

785
01:28:55.848 --> 01:28:57.357
I see.

786
01:29:01.562 --> 01:29:05.115
Governor Odious with Nurse Evelyn!

787
01:29:08.444 --> 01:29:10.203
She's right.

788
01:29:23.542 --> 01:29:25.343
She's right!

789
01:29:35.179 --> 01:29:37.472
We don't need her.

790
01:29:37.473 --> 01:29:39.524
She can't be trusted.

791
01:29:41.477 --> 01:29:46.406
You give them your heart,
but all they really want is your wallet.

792
01:29:47.691 --> 01:29:51.402
Sooner or later she's gonna leave him
for a richer man.

793
01:29:51.403 --> 01:29:52.737
Is a trap.

794
01:29:52.738 --> 01:29:56.157
<i>- I understand.</i>
- I don't like it.

795
01:29:56.158 --> 01:29:58.502
<i>Thank you for telling me.</i>

796
01:30:00.496 --> 01:30:03.381
Is a suicide. For all of us.

797
01:30:05.459 --> 01:30:07.344
We're going.

798
01:30:11.798 --> 01:30:15.936
Hey, Indian, what means suicide?

799
01:31:10.691 --> 01:31:13.034
Wallace? Wallace!

800
01:31:17.948 --> 01:31:19.541
Wallace!

801
01:31:19.908 --> 01:31:22.410
Wallace, what are you doing?

802
01:31:22.411 --> 01:31:25.255
Wallace, please will you come down?

803
01:31:26.498 --> 01:31:29.458
Please, this really isn't the time.

804
01:31:29.459 --> 01:31:32.220
Wallace, please!
Wallace, will you come down?

805
01:31:34.756 --> 01:31:36.308
Wallace!

806
01:31:42.848 --> 01:31:44.357
Wallace!

807
01:31:48.478 --> 01:31:50.822
Wallace, what did you do?

808
01:31:59.865 --> 01:32:02.459
<i>Americana Exotica!</i>

809
01:32:04.703 --> 01:32:06.838
<i>Americana Exotica!</i>

810
01:32:07.706 --> 01:32:09.674
It's beautiful!

811
01:32:19.926 --> 01:32:22.854
<i>Does he really died?</i>

812
01:32:34.650 --> 01:32:36.326
Let's go!

813
01:32:37.152 --> 01:32:38.527
I'm all washed-up!

814
01:32:38.528 --> 01:32:41.489
- Uncle Darwin, there's angry people.
- Don't leave me, my friend.

815
01:32:41.490 --> 01:32:44.751
I'll tell everyone they were your idea.

816
01:32:45.327 --> 01:32:48.338
They're going to find out I'm a fraud!

817
01:32:51.917 --> 01:32:54.302
Go on! Shoot, you animals!

818
01:32:56.922 --> 01:32:59.933
They'll pay you well for Darwin's hide.

819
01:33:12.354 --> 01:33:14.239
<i>He died, too.</i>

820
01:33:15.565 --> 01:33:17.409
<i>And Wallace, too?</i>

821
01:33:18.568 --> 01:33:20.194
Did he really died?

822
01:33:20.195 --> 01:33:24.124
Yeah, and in Wallace's case, happily so.

823
01:33:26.118 --> 01:33:28.169
It was the natural order of things.

824
01:33:38.463 --> 01:33:40.557
<i>All things must die.</i>

825
01:33:52.477 --> 01:33:54.195
Damn it all!

826
01:34:18.837 --> 01:34:21.806
Back! Get back!

827
01:35:03.173 --> 01:35:04.849
Kaboom.

828
01:35:39.376 --> 01:35:41.585
If you want something done...

829
01:35:41.586 --> 01:35:43.254
Get down there!

830
01:35:43.255 --> 01:35:45.130
...you have to do it yourself.

831
01:35:45.131 --> 01:35:47.550
Get down there, you animals!

832
01:35:47.551 --> 01:35:49.727
And bring them up here!

833
01:35:57.269 --> 01:36:01.239
<i>I don't like this! I don't like this story.</i>

834
01:36:02.774 --> 01:36:05.076
Why are we running away?

835
01:36:15.287 --> 01:36:18.664
<i>Why did Luigi kill himself?</i>

836
01:36:18.665 --> 01:36:21.667
<i>Why did not he come with us?</i>

837
01:36:21.668 --> 01:36:23.761
<i>And live as half a man?</i>

838
01:36:26.131 --> 01:36:28.132
He couldn't do that.

839
01:36:28.133 --> 01:36:30.059
He gave up.

840
01:36:30.594 --> 01:36:33.637
It's not very satisfying, is it?

841
01:36:33.638 --> 01:36:36.065
He didn't think so either.

842
01:36:45.442 --> 01:36:47.276
Please, the Mystic.

843
01:36:47.277 --> 01:36:50.914
Why? Why are they killing the Mystic?

844
01:36:53.074 --> 01:36:55.335
We need to go help him.

845
01:37:00.916 --> 01:37:02.333
Mystic!

846
01:37:02.334 --> 01:37:04.835
- Hey!
- Mystic!

847
01:37:04.836 --> 01:37:09.182
Googly, googly, googly, googly,
googly, googly.

848
01:37:49.589 --> 01:37:52.517
I'm sorry! I'm sorry!

849
01:37:54.761 --> 01:37:56.604
I'm sorry!

850
01:37:59.557 --> 01:38:01.401
I'm sorry!

851
01:38:07.315 --> 01:38:09.033
I'm sorry.

852
01:38:10.819 --> 01:38:14.038
Googly, googly, googly!

853
01:38:21.287 --> 01:38:22.922
It's okay.

854
01:39:15.967 --> 01:39:17.602
Indian!

855
01:39:24.601 --> 01:39:25.809
Up!

856
01:39:25.810 --> 01:39:27.278
Help!

857
01:39:43.036 --> 01:39:45.829
No, no, no, no, no.

858
01:39:45.830 --> 01:39:47.757
No, no, no, no!

859
01:39:54.839 --> 01:39:57.475
Why are you killing everybody?

860
01:39:59.677 --> 01:40:02.346
Why are you making everybody die?

861
01:40:02.347 --> 01:40:04.056
It's my story.

862
01:40:04.057 --> 01:40:05.691
Mine too.

863
01:40:09.354 --> 01:40:11.322
<i>Bring them up here!</i>

864
01:40:13.525 --> 01:40:15.692
Alive!

865
01:40:15.693 --> 01:40:17.412
We are here.

866
01:40:20.782 --> 01:40:22.417
Alive.

867
01:40:25.620 --> 01:40:27.130
Roy!

868
01:40:28.498 --> 01:40:30.749
<i>Don't look at her.</i>

869
01:40:30.750 --> 01:40:34.262
<i>- She is also with Odious.
- Quiet.</i>

870
01:40:36.256 --> 01:40:39.842
<i>- Just like your girlfriend.
- Shut up.</i>

871
01:40:39.843 --> 01:40:41.593
No!

872
01:40:41.594 --> 01:40:45.305
<i>Your girlfriend came with Odious
to see you...</i>

873
01:40:45.306 --> 01:40:47.224
<i>The bandit entered Odious's garden...</i>

874
01:40:47.225 --> 01:40:50.310
<i>But she stood in the car and she...</i>

875
01:40:50.311 --> 01:40:54.398
<i>- But Odious was nowhere to be seen.
- And Odious...</i>

876
01:40:54.399 --> 01:40:59.495
As the bandit ran past Odious' hiding place,
Odious cracked him in the nose!

877
01:41:04.075 --> 01:41:07.128
<i>No, but wait a little. Wait, please!</i>

878
01:41:14.669 --> 01:41:18.055
<i>So he sank to the bottom of the pool.</i>

879
01:41:19.090 --> 01:41:21.559
<i>He didn't even try to swim.</i>

880
01:41:21.926 --> 01:41:25.396
- You are making this up.
- No, I'm not.

881
01:41:26.347 --> 01:41:28.774
And he started to sink and he was dying.

882
01:41:30.268 --> 01:41:32.069
<i>Let him live.</i>

883
01:41:33.688 --> 01:41:35.105
Get up!

884
01:41:35.106 --> 01:41:37.408
Roy, get up and fight!

885
01:41:37.901 --> 01:41:39.452
Get up!

886
01:41:41.321 --> 01:41:44.948
Oh, what a shame! Look, God damn it!

887
01:41:44.949 --> 01:41:46.501
Get up!

888
01:41:48.036 --> 01:41:50.621
Look at him! Look at him!

889
01:41:50.622 --> 01:41:51.705
Get up!

890
01:41:51.706 --> 01:41:54.833
- I want you to see how pathetic he really is.
- I can't get up!

891
01:41:54.834 --> 01:41:56.627
- Get up!
- I can't get up!

892
01:41:56.628 --> 01:41:58.754
- For God's sake, the water's only waist high.
- Get up, Daddy!

893
01:41:58.755 --> 01:41:59.963
I'm not your father.

894
01:41:59.964 --> 01:42:03.842
How pathetic! Look at him!
He's a drug addict!

895
01:42:03.843 --> 01:42:06.136
Your father is a coward.

896
01:42:06.137 --> 01:42:08.472
A useless good-for-nothing!

897
01:42:08.473 --> 01:42:10.057
Dad, get up!

898
01:42:10.058 --> 01:42:11.850
He can't win!

899
01:42:11.851 --> 01:42:14.820
That's because
our Masked Bandit's a coward!

900
01:42:15.313 --> 01:42:18.199
Yeah, he never took an oath.

901
01:42:18.900 --> 01:42:21.985
- A fake, he's a liar and a coward.
- You're lying!

902
01:42:21.986 --> 01:42:24.956
<i>No. He had his fingers crossed.</i>

903
01:42:25.990 --> 01:42:27.333
He has to die.

904
01:42:27.992 --> 01:42:30.044
<i>I don't believe you.</i>

905
01:42:32.914 --> 01:42:34.674
<i>He was dying.</i>

906
01:42:35.458 --> 01:42:37.093
<i>Don't kill him.</i>

907
01:42:37.961 --> 01:42:41.838
<i>- I 'll bring you more pills if you want.</i>
- Dad, get up!

908
01:42:41.839 --> 01:42:44.883
- Don't kill him.
- There's nothing left for him.

909
01:42:44.884 --> 01:42:46.134
His daughter.

910
01:42:46.135 --> 01:42:48.646
He wasn't her father, either.

911
01:42:49.138 --> 01:42:51.107
She loves him.

912
01:42:52.225 --> 01:42:55.727
She'll survive. She's young.

913
01:42:55.728 --> 01:42:58.114
I don't want you to die.

914
01:43:08.408 --> 01:43:10.376
Don't kill him.

915
01:43:20.044 --> 01:43:21.846
Let him live.

916
01:43:25.300 --> 01:43:27.101
Let him live.

917
01:43:27.719 --> 01:43:29.562
<i>Don't kill him.</i>

918
01:43:40.690 --> 01:43:44.901
Promise? And don't cross your fingers.

919
01:43:44.902 --> 01:43:46.829
I promise.

920
01:43:47.071 --> 01:43:49.123
Show me your hands.

921
01:43:52.785 --> 01:43:54.128
See?

922
01:44:01.252 --> 01:44:03.387
<i>No more fighting.</i>

923
01:44:05.006 --> 01:44:08.842
<i>He needs to go to his daughter.
It's okay.</i>

924
01:44:08.843 --> 01:44:12.021
It's okay. It's all right. It's over now.

925
01:44:14.766 --> 01:44:16.651
Give me a kiss.

926
01:44:35.828 --> 01:44:37.588
Roy,

927
01:44:38.122 --> 01:44:42.927
you do realize it was all a test
to see if you truly loved me, don't you?

928
01:44:54.514 --> 01:44:57.608
We're finally free to follow our hearts.

929
01:45:04.899 --> 01:45:06.701
By all means.

930
01:45:10.488 --> 01:45:12.498
Follow your heart.

931
01:45:18.579 --> 01:45:20.965
I'm not feeling very well.

932
01:45:34.846 --> 01:45:37.106
We're a strange pair, aren't we?

933
01:45:52.363 --> 01:45:55.166
Action, action, action, action.

934
01:46:57.261 --> 01:46:59.804
So, this is the kind of trash
we're gonna be making now.

935
01:46:59.805 --> 01:47:04.652
People jumping off buildings,
bridges, horses.

936
01:47:37.426 --> 01:47:39.770
Did I just miss something?

937
01:47:41.639 --> 01:47:43.431
That was it?

938
01:47:43.432 --> 01:47:45.693
That was his big stunt?

939
01:47:46.143 --> 01:47:48.988
He didn't even use that horse thing.

940
01:48:37.778 --> 01:48:42.866
<i>I put old man's teeth there
because I think that</i>

941
01:48:42.867 --> 01:48:48.038
<i>the Mystic comes out of the tree
and it will grow a special orange tree.</i>

942
01:48:48.039 --> 01:48:50.758
Alexandria! Alexandria!

943
01:48:55.463 --> 01:49:00.768
<i>And we'll have oranges inside with teeths,
with teeth inside.</i>

944
01:49:16.067 --> 01:49:20.746
<i>When I get out from the hospital,
I miss Roy very much.</i>

945
01:49:22.031 --> 01:49:25.992
<i>My mother told me that he plays in pictures</i>

946
01:49:25.993 --> 01:49:29.496
<i>and he does things
that the other actors cannot do</i>

947
01:49:29.497 --> 01:49:32.716
<i>like falling and hitting</i>

948
01:49:34.919 --> 01:49:38.472
<i>and when they climb on something,
when they...</i>

949
01:49:40.299 --> 01:49:45.020
<i>I didn't believe my mother,
but then I saw him.</i>

950
01:49:53.270 --> 01:49:58.358
<i>I watch the picture again
and again and again</i>

951
01:49:58.359 --> 01:50:02.329
<i>and to make sure that was Roy,
and was Roy!</i>

952
01:50:05.449 --> 01:50:09.661
<i>And then, I like the action
from all the pictures</i>

953
01:50:09.662 --> 01:50:15.462
<i>because I know that Roy is making
all the falling and hitting and climbing</i>

954
01:50:16.377 --> 01:50:17.961
<i>and he was on the stairs</i>

955
01:50:17.962 --> 01:50:21.756
<i>and he was going up and down
and up and down.</i>

956
01:50:21.757 --> 01:50:27.657
<i>And he was falling from the train
and he was taking the car...</i>

957
01:51:00.254 --> 01:51:03.381
<i>And he was falling from the bicycle
and from a big house.</i>

958
01:51:03.382 --> 01:51:04.549
<i>It was Wallace!</i>

959
01:51:04.550 --> 01:51:06.217
<i>He was falling with the rope</i>

960
01:51:06.218 --> 01:51:09.063
<i>and he was hit and he was going...</i>

961
01:51:10.765 --> 01:51:14.651
<i>"Thank you, thank you,
thank you very much!"</i>
